<Fig2>

The zoomed XRD pattern around the (002) diffraction peak of PMN--PT(001) substrate shows the high epitaxy quality of 20 nm NiO thin film, as shown in #link(<Fig1>)[1]\(a). We then decreased the thickness of NiO film and fabricated Pt(3 nm)/NiO(3 u.c.)/PMN--PT(001) heterostructure (u.c. is the abbreviation of unit cells), in which the AFM--PM transition is around RT @Liang2023. The surface morphology of Pt(3 nm)/NiO(3 u.c.)/PMN--PT(001) heterostructure is shown in #link(<SF2>)[6], Supplementary Materials, revealing a roughness of about 700 pm. The AHE and resistivity measurements were then conducted in a Hall bar device with measurement current $I_(upright("measure"))$ of 0.5 mA applied along the in-plane \[100\] direction, corresponding to a current density of about 8.3$times 10^5 thin upright("A/cm")^2$ about two orders lower than the value for substaintial spin-orbit torque effects @ChenxzSwitching2018@moriyama2018spin, as schematically shown in #link(<Fig1>)[1]\(b). By applying $E_(upright("gate")) = plus.minus 4$ kV/cm, the PMN--PT substrate can be poled into opposite ferroelectric polarization $P$. This electric field is homogeneously out-of-plane, minimizing the possible spin accumulation induced by in-plane electric field @cai2017electric. After poling of the PMN--PT substrate, the $E_(upright("gate"))$ was removed and PMN--PT substrate relaxed into two remnant states with ferroelectric polarization about $plus.minus$20 $mu upright("C") \/ upright("cm")^2$ (noted as states $P_arrow.t$ and $P_arrow.b$, respectively), see polarization-electric field hysteresis loop in #link(<SF3>)[7], Supplementary Materials. The resistivity variation of the device was confirmed to be less than 0.4% between $P_arrow.t$ and $P_arrow.b$ states, as shown in #link(<SF4>)[8], Supplementary Materials. The AHE resistance $R_(upright("AHE"))$ was monitored by sweeping the out-of-plane external magnetic field $mu_0 H$ at RT for the states $P_arrow.t$ and $P_arrow.b$, as shown in #link(<Fig1>)[1]\(c). It should be noted that the Hall data is an odd function as the sweeping magnetic field, avoiding the mixing of magnetoresistance, which is an even function. The ordinary Hall effect background induced by Lorentz force has been subtracted with coefficient about $3.7 times 10^(- 7) thin Omega thin upright("Oe")^(- 1)$ for the states $P_arrow.t$ and $3.6 times 10^(- 7) thin Omega thin upright("Oe")^(- 1)$ for the states $P_arrow.b$, respectively (see #link(<SF5>)[9] in Supplementary Materials for the raw Hall resistance results). It clearly shows the non-volatile electric-field control of AHE, as the saturated $R_(upright("AHE"))$ for $P_arrow.t$ and $P_arrow.b$ states is 7.5~m$Omega$ and 10~m$Omega$, respectively.

